<title>SRI LANKA: WEATHER-LIGHT SHOWERS SEEN OVER PARTS OF S.LANKA.</title>
<headline>WEATHER-LIGHT SHOWERS SEEN OVER PARTS OF S.LANKA.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-08-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department forecast light showers at a few places in the central, Western, Sabaragamuwa and Southern provinces for Monday.</p>
<p>It said isolated thundershowers are likely in the Uva and east during Monday afternoon or evening.</p>
<p>It released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Sunday morning:</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Canyon		   18.7</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	    14.9</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   0.6</p>
<p>    Laxapana		 11.1</p>
<p>    Moussakele		2.2</p>
<p>    Norton		    0</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
</text>
